Subject: [PATCH] speech: profile voices spoken by a real local engine

speechSynthesis.getVoices() returns the profile's voice list. A voice
that matches a host voice uses that voice as is, and any other is spoken
by a host voice of the same language, then the same primary language,
then the first available. A page sees the profile's names, languages and
flags, and speech runs on a real engine with real events. Otherwise a
Windows profile on a Mac lists the Mac's own voices, or an empty list
that no desktop Chrome reports.

